= Docs: jesp diamonds 4-8 and the Truffle-only plan; the sweep gates at 3
The + loop: add_I sited 285 -> 189 ns (the small-int cache is noise, off); frame-free callees 142;
hllize sited, checkarity off the boundary 123; frame-free across languages 83-92; the boundaries
gone and the loader walking simple graphemes take the cold gate 126 -> 90 s. Diamond 7 costs the
compiler nothing; the stage0 refresh does not change stage2; run-once code pays the DSL interpreter
tier (plan item 4). The Truffle-only plan ranked; item 1 rewritten around the plain sub call; HLL
simplification sliced; dispatching-blocks-frame-free deferred; gates at 3, the sweep budgets like the server's guard.
